{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1145757-ultimate-survivalist","id":1145757,"title":"Ultimate Survivalist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-01T04:35:38-07:00","id":1145757,"title":"Ultimate Survivalist","content":"I like making resilient characters, especially in settings where food shortage might become a problem or where traveling for long times through harsh conditions is a given.<br /> And since playing with other people is more fun and an additional pair of eyes spots things one would otherwise overlook, I wanted to ask you how you would build your most resilient starting character. Just to clarify: this is not meant to be a fighting character that can take damage, but rather someone who is able to survive in harsh conditions that you can't necessarily punch in the face. I want a char that can be thrown into the woods/Antarctic/Desert/Jungle/Plains for whatever task (be it &quot;Survive for a month and you get what you want&quot;) with little to no preperation and still make it through.<br /> <br /> High Survival and Hardy are a given here, really, and Survivalist is also often a good choice. Parkour also makes some sense. Crafts is something every survivalist will want to pick up. The rest are probably more character-specific.<br /> In my opinion, Beasts and Prometheans are clear favourites here (because of course they are, I am biased towards thinking that and freely acknowledge that =P ).<br /> Beasts are likely to get a bunch of immunities thanks to Atavisms and Lair Traits, and Prometheans have very helpful merits and are resilient by nature.<br /> A Promethean with the Acid Stomach and Sleepless Merits has a big advantage, but it really comes together with Motus: Sleepless and Motus stack and turn the Promethean into a sort of perpetual mobile who no longer needs to worry about things like sleep and food as long as they are moving. Burning Pyros on Motus helps with moving very, very fast (Motus 3 gives +3 Str, +1 Dext and doubles speed). This would necessitate a Titan or Sentry, so a Titan is the more likely choice here, which is fine, as it gives access to Vitality. Unbroken with the additional Stamina is the more useful choice here, I think, as it also allows ignoring physical Tilts/Conditions for 2 Pyros. A Tammuz with Heart of Clay is probably the most sensible choice here (exceptional successes to resist stuff at 3 successes is nice) and other sensible Merits are Efficient Conductor and Moth to the Flame. The real winner is Weatherproof, though: this allows the character to withstand and cross areas that would be otherwise far too dangerous. Put everything together, you get a character than can run through a desert for days on end, and can sustain themselves with basically everything they find (sand, pieces of wood, soil, stones) should they have to stay in one place for a long time.<br /> A Beast might be less impressive, but with Advanced Orientation, Patient and Good Time Management we have a good base for Merits and/or hunting/scavenging (less Beast-Specific though).<br /> Storm-Lashed and Relentless Hunter help, although something like Infestation might be more useful than Relentless Hunter, depending on what this character explores (caves or underwater? Definitly Infestation) Infestation also offers additional mobility for a satiety. Relentless Hunter helps with sustaining yourself even on slightly poisonous things and resist sickness, whereas with Storm-Lashed a big part of nature's dangers in the form of sudden gusts of wind and lighting become harmless. Later on, the character will want to pick up Needs Must for improved Eyesight/hearing etc, but for now being able to make your own weather is a huge boon. So I'd go with Infestation/Storm-Lashed. This puts us towards either Namtaru or Ugallu, of which I definitly choose Ugallu for their Birthright. Finding hidden food (like, say, animals) is a huge boon to help sustaining yourself.<br /> Good Lair traits are easy to come by: from Extreme Heat/Cold, to Blizzard, to Downpour, to Burning and Darkness, or even going so far as getting Toxic or Diseased - they all offer great benefits regarding survivability.<br /> <br /> All in all, a Beast must be more tailored towards the specific area and thus is a specialist, whereas the Promethean char is more of a generalist character.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, what is your favourite Bear-Grylls-goes-ChroD concept? Pitch me your Kindred (my money's on Gangrel Dragons), Uratha (Storm-Lord Irraka?), your Changelings and Unchained! =D<br /> Your Beast or Promethean setup is better than mine? Show me!<br /> (Mages should be excluded, because Mages usually win, but since this is CharCreation only I'd say throw me your Mages =D)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 10-01-2017, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T06:38:28-07:00","id":1145779,"title":"","content":"Problem with Beast or Vampire is gonna be how they will feed to keep up these survivalist powers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T08:06:14-07:00","id":1145794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1145757-ultimate-survivalist?p=1145779#post1145779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem with Beast or Vampire is gonna be how they will feed to keep up these survivalist powers</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Beast might have an advantage here due to less steep loss of satiety, but Demons and others would not even have to deal with that. But yeah, my Chosen abilities could be a drain, so replacing storm-lashed With dragonbreath (Easy Access To Fire is Good + Immune To flames) Might Be A Good idea.<br /> I stand by infestation for areas with tight places or water, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: actually though, a kindred might find animals on which they could feed, same as others could Hunt to sustain themselves, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 10-01-2017, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T08:19:11-07:00","id":1145797,"title":"","content":"I'd say Mages, Mummies, Demons and Prometheans are probably going to have the edge here. Mages just have such a broad toolbox (Forces, Matter and Life would be most immediately useful here), Mummies are immortal, god-like beings with at least a couple powers that produce incredbly fecund places (gotta feed the vult, y'know), Demons have several toolboxes to play with with their covers, Embeds, Exploits and Form powers, plus the fact that they don't strictly need to eat. Prometheans have extreme durability, they can eat nearly anything, and they have all those cool alchemical powers, some of which can be very useful for surviving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T10:48:09-07:00","id":1146100,"title":"","content":"I actually prefer Werewolves for this sort of thing, but am away from books to highlight the advantages/disadvantages...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T12:37:52-07:00","id":1146126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1145757-ultimate-survivalist?p=1145797#post1145797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">plus the fact that they don't strictly need to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they feel all the same urges as their Cover, and it requires fuel and tune-ups (food and exercise and such)? Maybe their Demonic form doesn't need to eat, but I doubt the God-Machine couldn't screw with you even in the deep wilderness if stories got around about some giant biomechanical monster tromping around","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}